# Replication package

*Oil Price Shocks, Sovereign Risk, and Bank Interest Rates Under Full Dollarization: Evidence From Ecuador*

## One command

```bash
bash run_all.sh                    # every table and figure, from raw data (about 2 hours)
UPDATE_DATA=1 bash run_all.sh      # fetch the current data vintages instead (results will differ from the paper)
```

Random seeds are fixed in every script that draws from a posterior or a Monte Carlo distribution. Results were produced with R 4.6.1 and Python 3.14 on Windows 11.

## Software

| Language | Packages |
|---|---|
| R (≥ 4.3) | seasonal 1.11.0 and x13binary (X-13ARIMA-SEATS), urca, strucchange, ggplot2. All VAR, Bayesian (Normal–inverse-Wishart Minnesota prior), counterfactual, historical-decomposition and local-projection routines are purpose-written in `src/var_functions.R` and `src/pipeline_functions.R`; no VAR package is used. |
| Python (≥ 3.10) | pandas, numpy, openpyxl, tabulate (data and tables); matplotlib (Figure 1); python-docx and pandoc ≥ 3 (manuscript build only; the manuscript text is not in the repository until acceptance, and that step is skipped without it) |

Versions used for the reported results: R 4.6.1 with seasonal 1.11.0, x13binary 1.1.61.2, urca 1.3.4, strucchange 1.6.0, ggplot2 4.0.3; Python 3.14.7 with pandas 3.0.5, numpy 2.5.2, openpyxl 3.1.5, tabulate 0.10.0, matplotlib 3.11.1, python-docx 1.2.0; pandoc 3.11. Random seeds are set at the top of `src/04`, `06`, `08`, `08b`, `08c` and `09`; the remaining scripts reuse the saved posterior draws. The literature search strings and dates are in `literature/search_log.md`.

No interactive software is used.

## Data (all public)

The Baumeister–Hamilton shock series is revised and extended periodically at its source (the paper uses the vintage ending in 2026:03, retrieved 2026-09-26). To reproduce the paper exactly, the repository ships the vintages used, with attribution to their authors; by default the pipeline downloads only the VIX, whose historical daily values are not revised. `data/raw/SHA256SUMS.txt` records the SHA-256 checksum of every raw file shipped (`cd data/raw && sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.txt`). The VIX is not redistributed: `src/01_fetch_fred.py` downloads it and reports whether its daily values through 2026-09-22 match those used in the paper.

| File | Content | Source |
|---|---|---|
| `data/raw/BCE_Dataset_Unificado_Mensual_companion.csv` (included) | Ecuadorian crude price, international reserves, M2, EMBI (corrected), reference deposit and lending rates, EFFR, private credit, monetary base, inflation; monthly | Banco Central del Ecuador statistical portal, compiled by the author; the EMBI thousands-separator correction is described in Section 3.1 of the paper |
| `data/raw/FRED_*.csv` (vintages used in the paper, included; the VIX file is downloaded) | CPIAUCSL, VIXCLS, POILBREUSDM, MCOILWTICO, FEDFUNDS | Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis, FRED; downloaded by `src/01_fetch_fred.py` (log in `data/raw/FRED_download_log.txt`). VIX is © Cboe, distributed through FRED |
| `data/raw/oil_shocks/BH_oil_supply_shocks.xlsx`, `BH_oil_demand_shocks.xlsx` (vintage used in the paper, included) | Structural oil supply and demand shocks, vintage 1975:02–2026:03 | Baumeister & Hamilton (2019), https://sites.google.com/site/cjsbaumeister/datasets; downloaded by `src/00_fetch_oil_shocks.py`. Later vintages may revise values |
| `data/raw/oil_shocks/Kaenzig_oilSupplyNewsShocks_2025M12.xlsx` (vintage used in the paper, included) | Oil supply news shocks, vintage 2025M12 | Känzig (2021), https://github.com/dkaenzig/oilsupplynews; downloaded by `src/00_fetch_oil_shocks.py` |

Processed files are rebuilt by the pipeline: `data/processed/oil_channel_monthly_full.csv`, `oil_channel_monthly.csv` (VAR-ready, 2007:08–2026:06), `oil_shocks_monthly.csv`. Data issues and choices (U.S. CPI 2025:10 interpolation, constant-rate period 2011:10–2014:04, reserve outliers) are documented in `data/README_data.md`.

## Scripts and outputs

| Script | Produces |
|---|---|
| `src/00_fetch_oil_shocks.py` | Oil supply shock files |
| `src/01_fetch_fred.py` | FRED raw files |
| `src/02_build_dataset.py` | Merged dataset, real oil prices, monthly VIX |
| `src/03_seasonal_adjust.R` | X-13 adjustment of reserves and M2; `output/tables/x13_diagnostics.csv` |
| `src/03b_plot_data.R` | Optional visual check of the VAR series (`output/figures/check_var_series.png`); not a paper figure and not run by `run_all.sh` |
| `src/05_oil_shocks.py` | External shock series merged; relevance checks |
| `src/04_var_baseline.R` | Recursive VAR, lag tests (Table S2), Minnesota λ, posterior draws |
| `src/06_var_oil_supply_shocks.R` | VARs with the Baumeister–Hamilton and Känzig shocks (Table 4, Table S5, Figure 3) |
| `src/07_counterfactuals.R` | Route decomposition, marginal contributions by order and credibility diagnostics (Tables 5, 6, S6, S7, S13; Figure 4, Figure S3) |
| `src/07b_stable_draws.R` | Decomposition on dynamically stable posterior draws (Table S14) |
| `src/07c_shapley_inference.R` | Posterior comparison of the Shapley attributions and routes over horizons 1–12 (Table S16) |
| `src/07d_model_diagnostics.R` | Residual diagnostics and posterior distribution of the credibility statistics (Tables S20 and S21) |
| `src/08_robustness.R` | Robustness specifications, Shapley attributions and VIX scenarios (Tables 8, S3, S8, S9, S10, S12; Figure S4). Each specification is cached in `output/models/robust_cache`, so the script can be interrupted and rerun; `ROBUST_MINUTES=10 Rscript src/08_robustness.R` limits each call to about ten minutes |
| `src/08b_common_sample.R` | The three identifications on the common sample 2008:08–2025:12 (Table S17) |
| `src/08c_fixed_rate_period.R` | Post-fixed-rate samples with four lags, one dummy per fixed-rate month, and higher residual variance in crisis months (Table S19) |
| `src/09_historical_decomposition.R` | Historical decomposition (Tables 7, S15; Figures 5, S5) |
| `src/10_local_projections.R` | LP-IV estimates, including private credit (also with calendar-month fixed effects) and inflation, and conditional first-stage F statistics (Tables S4, S11; Figure S2) |
| `src/11_descriptives.R` | Descriptive statistics, unit roots, instrument checks (Tables 3, S1, S4) |
| `src/11b_kpss_breaks.R` | KPSS tests on first differences with Bai–Perron mean breaks (note to Table S1; requires strucchange) |
| `src/12_figures.R` | Figures 2–5 and S1–S5, 350 dpi PNG and vector PDF (`output/figures/paper/`) |
| `src/12b_route_schematic.py` | Figure 1, schematic of the transmission routes (requires matplotlib) |
| `src/13_tables.py` | All tables as APA-formatted markdown (`paper/_tables/`), including Table S18 (identifying assumptions), which it writes directly |
| `paper/build_docx.py`, `paper/build_elsevier.py` | APA manuscript and Elsevier submission files (`paper/submission/`); added with the manuscript text after acceptance |

Intermediate numerical results are in `output/tables/*.csv`; posterior draws are saved in `output/models/*.rds` (large; regenerated by the pipeline).
# Data log — oil liquidity channel (built 2026-09-26)

## Pipeline
1. `python src/01_fetch_fred.py`: downloads CPIAUCSL, VIXCLS, POILBREUSDM, MCOILWTICO and FEDFUNDS to `data/raw/` (log in `FRED_download_log.txt`).
2. `python src/02_build_dataset.py`: merges them with `data/raw/BCE_Dataset_Unificado_Mensual_companion.csv` (a copy of the companion project's processed dataset). Deflates oil prices to USD of June 2026, averages VIX to monthly, builds the log transforms. Writes `processed/oil_channel_monthly_full.csv` (2000:01–2026:09) and `processed/oil_channel_monthly_raw.csv`.
3. `Rscript src/03_seasonal_adjust.R`: X-13ARIMA-SEATS on reserves and M2 over 2000:01–2026:07. Writes `processed/oil_channel_monthly.csv` (**VAR-ready, 2007:08–2026:06, T = 227**) and `output/tables/x13_diagnostics.csv`.
4. `Rscript src/03b_plot_data.R`: visual check, `output/figures/check_var_series.png`.

## VAR variables (processed/oil_channel_monthly.csv)
`l_oil_ecu_real`, `effr`, `l_vix`, `l_reserves`, `l_m2`, `embi` (pp), `deposit_rate`, `lending_rate` (plus `spread` and robustness series). Log variables are 100 × log.

## Checks passed
- No missing values in the estimation window for any VAR variable.
- The companion `effr_prom` equals FRED FEDFUNDS exactly (max abs diff 0).
- Ecuadorian crude vs. Brent correlation 0.988, vs. WTI 0.970 (2007:08–2026:06).
- X-13: significant seasonality before adjustment (QS p = 0.034 reserves, < 0.001 M2), none after (p = 1).

## Issues found (need a decision or a note in the paper)
1. **U.S. CPI for 2025:10 is missing in FRED** (the figure was never published). It is filled by log-linear interpolation between 2025:09 and 2025:11 (324.654). Affects only the oil deflator for one month.
2. **Deposit and lending reference rates are constant for 31 months, 2011:10–2014:04** (4.53% and 8.17%). This is not a data error in the merge; the values come unchanged from the BCE series. A stretch with zero variance in the outcome variables affects any VAR. Options: (a) a dummy for the period; (b) baseline sample from 2014:05 (about 146 observations); (c) keep the full sample and report (b) as robustness. The cause (administered reference rates vs. methodology) should be documented from BCE sources before choosing. The companion paper does not appear to discuss this stretch.
3. **Reserves have large non-oil jumps.** X-13 flags 12 outliers (e.g., LS 2011:02, AO 2017:09, AO 2017:12, AO 2020:03, LS 2020:10); the log change is +0.85 in 2018:01 and +0.71 in 2017:10. These are likely external bond issuances and multilateral disbursements, not oil, and they are kept in the adjusted series because they are genuine movements. They support (i) the use of M2 alongside reserves, and (ii) controlling for, or identifying, non-oil reserve shocks (Method, Robustness item 7).
4. **M2 is nominal and strongly trending** (log level rises about 200 points over the window). Options: include a deterministic trend in the VAR, deflate by U.S. CPI, or use M2/GDP (Carrillo-Maldonado et al., 2023). To be decided at the estimation stage.
5. The reserves series has not yet been confirmed as end-of-month stock vs. monthly average; check the BCE definition.
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# One-command replication of every table and figure in the paper and the Supplementary Material.
# Usage (from the project root):  bash run_all.sh            # full run (about 2 hours; step 08 dominates)
#                                 UPDATE_DATA=1 bash run_all.sh     # fetch current data vintages (results will differ from the paper)
#                                 SKIP_DOWNLOAD=1 bash run_all.sh   # no network access; needs data/raw/FRED_VIXCLS.csv
# Requirements: Python 3 (pandas, numpy, openpyxl, tabulate, matplotlib; python-docx for the manuscript build) and R >= 4.3
# (seasonal, x13binary, urca, strucchange, ggplot2). Set RSCRIPT if Rscript is not on the PATH.
set -euo pipefail
cd "$(dirname "$0")"
RSCRIPT="${RSCRIPT:-Rscript}"
PY="${PY:-python}"

step() { echo; echo "==== $1"; }

# Output directories that a fresh clone does not contain
mkdir -p data/raw/oil_shocks data/processed output/tables output/models output/figures/paper paper/_tables paper/submission

if [ "${SKIP_DOWNLOAD:-0}" != "1" ]; then
  step "00 Download oil supply shock series";    $PY src/00_fetch_oil_shocks.py
  step "01 Download FRED series";               $PY src/01_fetch_fred.py
fi
step "02 Build merged dataset";                 $PY src/02_build_dataset.py
step "03 X-13 seasonal adjustment";             $RSCRIPT src/03_seasonal_adjust.R
step "05 Merge external oil supply shocks";     $PY src/05_oil_shocks.py
step "04 Recursive baseline VAR (C0)";          $RSCRIPT src/04_var_baseline.R
step "06 VAR with oil supply shocks";           $RSCRIPT src/06_var_oil_supply_shocks.R
step "07 Counterfactual decomposition";         $RSCRIPT src/07_counterfactuals.R
step "07b Decomposition on stable draws";       $RSCRIPT src/07b_stable_draws.R
step "07c Comparison of the routes";           $RSCRIPT src/07c_shapley_inference.R
step "07d Residual and credibility diagnostics"; $RSCRIPT src/07d_model_diagnostics.R
step "08 Robustness and VIX scenarios";         $RSCRIPT src/08_robustness.R
step "08b Identifications on a common sample"; $RSCRIPT src/08b_common_sample.R
step "08c Fixed-rate period and crisis variance"; $RSCRIPT src/08c_fixed_rate_period.R
step "09 Historical decomposition";             $RSCRIPT src/09_historical_decomposition.R
step "10 Local projections (LP-IV)";            $RSCRIPT src/10_local_projections.R
step "11 Descriptives, unit roots, instruments"; $RSCRIPT src/11_descriptives.R
step "11b KPSS with breaks";                    $RSCRIPT src/11b_kpss_breaks.R
step "12 Figures";                              $RSCRIPT src/12_figures.R
step "12b Route schematic (Figure 1)";          $PY src/12b_route_schematic.py
step "13 Tables";                               $PY src/13_tables.py
# The manuscript text is added to the repository after acceptance; until then this step is skipped in a clone.
if [ -f paper/Introduction.md ]; then
  step "Manuscript (APA and Elsevier versions)"
  ( cd paper && $PY build_docx.py && $PY build_elsevier.py )
fi
echo; echo "Done. Tables: paper/_tables and output/tables; figures: output/figures/paper; manuscript (if its sources are present): paper/submission."
